From: relay12 contributors
Subject: [PATCH] dtl: make the interfaces range-flags variable a portable const

The same gap patch 0017 fixed in ResourceState.hpp recurs here:
llvm-mingw's winnt.h does not mark DEFINE_ENUM_FLAG_OPERATORS' operator|
constexpr, so a constexpr variable initialized through it is not a
constant expression under Clang, though it was under MSVC. This is a
function-local static, not a namespace-scope variable, but the same fix
applies: const preserves the exact linkage and one-time initialization
this local static already had, and needs only an ordinary initializer.

Both uses of InterfacesRangeFlags pass it as a runtime argument to
CD3DX12_DESCRIPTOR_RANGE1::Init, so nothing here depended on it being a
core constant expression.

A grep across every DEFINE_ENUM_FLAG_OPERATORS-declared type in both
DirectX-Headers and this project's own headers -- 119 distinct flag-enum
types in total -- found no other constexpr declaration of this shape
remaining in the tree.
---
diff --git a/src/RootSignature.cpp b/src/RootSignature.cpp
--- a/src/RootSignature.cpp
+++ b/src/RootSignature.cpp
@@ -49,7 +49,7 @@ namespace D3D12TranslationLayer
             RangeFlags |= D3D12_DESCRIPTOR_RANGE_FLAG_DESCRIPTORS_STATIC_KEEPING_BUFFER_BOUNDS_CHECKS;
         }
         // else STATIC (default)
-        static constexpr D3D12_DESCRIPTOR_RANGE_FLAGS InterfacesRangeFlags = D3D12_DESCRIPTOR_RANGE_FLAG_DATA_VOLATILE | D3D12_DESCRIPTOR_RANGE_FLAG_DESCRIPTORS_VOLATILE;
+        static const D3D12_DESCRIPTOR_RANGE_FLAGS InterfacesRangeFlags = D3D12_DESCRIPTOR_RANGE_FLAG_DATA_VOLATILE | D3D12_DESCRIPTOR_RANGE_FLAG_DESCRIPTORS_VOLATILE;
 
         UINT NumSRVRanges = std::accumulate(m_NumSRVSpacesUsed, std::end(m_NumSRVSpacesUsed), 0);
         CD3DX12_DESCRIPTOR_RANGE1* pSRVRanges;
